# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file is the lane split. A pull request touching any path below requires
# Hanna's approval. A pull request touching nothing below merges itself once
# the required checks pass.
#
# That is why the data refresh is allowed to be unattended: it only writes raw
# snapshots and published artefacts, neither of which is listed here. The
# moment a refresh tries to change a model, a registry, or a source, it lands
# in an owned path and stops for review.
#
# Do not add pipeline/data/ or web/public/data/ to this file. Doing so removes
# the zero-touch data lane entirely.

# Governing documents
/SPEC.md                    @hannasage
/CLAUDE.md                  @hannasage
/README.md                  @hannasage
/docs/                      @hannasage

# Agent configuration and enforcement
/.claude/                   @hannasage

# Continuous integration and automation
/.github/                   @hannasage
/scripts/                   @hannasage

# Data definitions. The transformations themselves, not their output.
/pipeline/ingest/           @hannasage
/pipeline/dbt/              @hannasage
/pipeline/registry/         @hannasage

# Application
/web/                       @hannasage

# Composite development. Reviewed by hand, always.
/notebooks/                 @hannasage

# Build configuration
/Makefile                   @hannasage
/pyproject.toml             @hannasage
/package.json               @hannasage
